	note = {arXiv:2205.13621 [cs]
TLDR: This work proposes a simple, easy to interpret, and computationally lightweight perturbation mechanism to be applied to an already trained model at the decoding stage, which is model-agnostic and can be used in conjunction with any LLM.},
	keywords = {Computer Science - Computation and Language, Computer Science - Machine Learning, Differential Privacy},
	annote = {
“DP-decoding [191] proposes a simple perturbation mechanism applied to the output probability distributions, which is sufficient for privacy guarantee due to the post-processing lemma [72].” (Deng 等, 2024, p. 8)
