	note = {arXiv:2401.12242 [cs]
TLDR: This paper proposes BadChain, the first backdoor attack against LLMs employing COT prompting, which does not require access to the training dataset or model parameters and imposes low computational overhead, and shows that LLMs endowed with stronger reasoning capabilities exhibit higher susceptibility to BadChain.},
	keywords = {Computer Science - Cryptography and Security, Computer Science - Machine Learning, Backdoor Attack, BadChain, Chain-of-Thought},
	annote = {Comment: Accepted to ICLR2024
