TLDR: This study comprehensively study the robustness of popular machine-generated text detectors under attacks from diverse categories: editing, paraphrasing, prompting, and co-generating and reveals that almost none of the existing detectors remain robust under all the attacks, and all detectors exhibit different loopholes.},
	keywords = {Computer Science - Computation and Language},
	annote = {“Meanwhile, further improvement on the watermark’s robustness to attack” (Deng 等, 2024, p. 12)
},
}

@misc{mitchell_detectgpt_2023,
